WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.140
A cactus in the Americas.

2
00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:04.230
A euphorbia in Africa.

3
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:09.900
They are unrelated, yet both have
spines and swollen, water-storing stems.

4
00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:15.130
Tropical forest grows in South America,
Central Africa and Southeast Asia.

5
00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:18.420
Different species, same type of community.

6
00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:21.110
So why do places on
opposite sides of the world,

7
00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:25.000
with no link between them,
end up looking so alike?

8
00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.950
In this mission, you'll
find out what a biome is,

9
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.800
and tour six of them, from
tundra to tropical forest.

10
00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:37.080
Then you'll dive onto a coral reef and
test the five conditions it needs to form.

11
00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:42.610
Your mission: explain why places with no
link between them end up looking so alike.
